From 2c35f3263d553d557f790caa64d0cf94fb5627df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pucawo <github@pucawo.de>
Date: Thu, 7 May 2026 00:08:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/9] fix(files): SSE heartbeat + emit-after-persist (codex
 review F1+F3+F4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three backend findings from the Phase-2 codex pass:

- F1 (statusStream): idle SSE connections used to send nothing between
  events, so a 30–60s proxy timeout (nginx/cloudflare) would force-close
  the connection. The bus has no replay, so any event during the
  reconnect window is lost. Fix: 25s ': heartbeat' comments, cleared
  in the same close/aborted path that drops bus listeners. Interval
  unref()'d so it doesn't keep the event loop alive on its own.
- F3 (inlinePipeline) / F4 (ragPipeline): safeEmit fired even when
  the underlying updateFile() returned null (file row vanished —
  TTL expired, user deleted) or rejected. The chip would then carry
  state the DB doesn't reflect. Fix: safeUpdateFile returns the doc
  on success, null otherwise; callers gate safeEmit on the truthy
  result.

Tests: 5 new heartbeat cases (emit, multi-emit, close-cleanup,
aborted-cleanup, post-end no-write) + 4 new emit-gate cases
(inline/rag × loaded-null/failed-throw). 19 existing pipeline tests
unchanged.
